  "front": {
   "note": "photo - the studio front photograph at ~1 px/mm vertically and ~1.1 horizontally: craft at y 15, EMI cover to 255, the upper cage (CB-RE0, SFB 0-7, CB-RE1) at y 269.9 over the guides' 412.1 mm, ten 43.18 mm slots over the line-card slots (#902; it was y 275 over ~405), the divider, the ten-slot lower cage at y 730 over ~425 mm, the LC 0-9 label strip, and the intake grille at the bottom. Cards are VERTICAL: authored tall with rotated jacks (the ASR-9010 pattern)"
  },
  "lc-slots": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "each LC slot is the line-card adapter's face, 43.18 x 449.8 (1.7 x 17.71 in, the guide's ADC row), on its own width as pitch: ten slots, 431.8 mm, centred on the chassis at x 4.1 (#261). Four readings put the pitch there: the MX2010 front gives 41.36 px between slots against a 379.5 px MPC plate, 43.3 mm on the card's 396.0; the MX2008 front, isotropic at 1.264 px/mm once its flanges are taken as the 19 in, gives 54.7 px, 43.3 mm; the MX2020 front gives 31.9 px at 0.744 px/mm, 43.4 mm. Until #261 the slots were an estimated 41.0 x 425.0 on a 41.0 pitch, which no adapter fits. The native MX2K cards and the blank keep their estimated 41 x 425 and are centred in the wider slot. Down: the slot is centred on the photograph's adapters, whose frame and handle blocks run 724 to 1163 px (729 to 1177 mm on the chassis scale, 0.981 px/mm from a 1483 px height): y 728.1. The divider above now ends at 728.1 and the LC label strip, its legends and the cover below move down to clear it, the strip at 1179.0 as the photograph has it (1181 to 1204)."
  },
